  <data name="label23.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>Bivalent-partial parallel operation is a mixture of bivalent-parallel and 
 Bivalent-alternative operation mode.
 The heat pump works alone up to the bivalence point and is then supported by the second heat generator. When another specified temperature is reached (e.g. -2 °C), the heat pump switches off.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="label22.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In the bivalent-parallel mode of operation, the heat requirement is borne solely by the heat pump until the bivalent point is reached. If the temperature falls below the bivalence point, the second heat generator supports the heating operation of the heat pump.</value>
  </data>
  <data name="label21.Text" xml:space="preserve">
    <value>In the bivalent-alternative mode of operation, the heat requirement is borne solely by the heat pump until the bivalent point is reached. The second heat generator steps in when the bivalence point is undershot and takes over sole heating operation.</value>
  </data>
